{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Living Longer Better", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Cream, Crust, Croutons", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Grammar - part 3 > Yes  Agnes", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 11, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe personal and regional eating habits and cooking in  a range of communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn6le11ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "craving", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a sudden and strong feeling for something  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: <br/> <span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: Do you have cravings? <br/> <span class=\"strong\">Joe</span>: Yes, for chocolate!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le11ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about cravings.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Expressing What Is Necessary", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the phrases <span class=\"italic\">have to</span> or <span class=\"italic\">have got to</span> to express what is necessary.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you pronounce these phrases in conversation, you can link and reduce the sounds. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <span class=\"italic\">Have to</span> sounds like <span class=\"italic\">hafta</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I hafta exercise. <br>She hasta eat chocolate.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Have got to</span> sounds like <span class=\"italic\">have gotta</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "He's gotta eat crunchy potato chips. <br>I've gotta do yoga.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice reading these examples aloud.", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Linking and Deletion with Superlatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use a superlative adjective to express the highest degree of a quality. You use a superlative adjective to talk about one thing or person in a group of things. You always use <span class=\"italic\">the</span> with the superlative.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In natural conversation, it is common to link and delete some sounds in the superlative adjective if there is a similar sound in the next word. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The biggest sweet tooth.  <Br>You delete the  <span class=\"italic\">t</span> sound and link the <span class=\"italic\">s</span> sound. <br>The bigges_sweet tooth.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sometimes this makes it hard to listen to native speakers talk.<br> If you know the rule, you can listen better. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice reading these words aloud:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The smallest sweater  =  The smalles_sweater <br>The loudest truck = The loudes_truck", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "cranberry", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small, dark red fruit with a bitter taste ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have a craving for cranberry muffins.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le11ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "crepe", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a round, flat, thin pancake ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love crepes for breakfast.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le11ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "croissant ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a crescent-shaped pastry; a popular French breakfast food ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love chocolate croissants!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le11ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "cranky", "type": "name"}, {"content": "easily upset; in a bad mood ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I get cranky when I have a craving.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le11ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "trigger", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that causes something else to happen ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Stress is a trigger for cravings.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le11ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "distraction", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that takes your attention away from something else ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Find a distraction to avoid giving in to cravings.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le11ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to meditate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to mentally relax by thinking about one thing ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A good distraction is to meditate.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le11ob04aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "outlet ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a release ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Exercise is a good outlet for stress.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le11ob04aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Write down 3 things you have a craving for.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down 3 ways you deal with the cravings.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss your points with your partner. Did you learn any other ways to deal with triggers?", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write down my cravings and how I deal with them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "My partner and I exchange information on how to deal with cravings.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn6le11ob04re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn6le11ob04re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "Do you have any cravings? Sometimes I just have to have a cranberry crepe from my favorite breakfast cafe. Or a bag of crunchy potato chips when I'm watching a movie. What about you? If you want to stay healthy, you've got to control your cravings. Here are some tips for getting those pesky habits under control:"}, {"image": "engenn6le11ob04re2img03.jpg", "time": "20000", "id": 2, "text": "<ol><li>Create a distraction. Cravings usually last for a short time so you've got to focus your attention on something else. Call someone, listen to music or exercise to take your mind off the craving.</li>\n<li>Avoid triggers. Try to change what you eat in general. The first few days are the hardest to deal with, but it gets easier. </li>\n<li>Since stress is one of the biggest triggers for cravings, find another way to relax. Meditate, do yoga, or exercise. You have to find an outlet for your stress.</li></ol>"}, {"image": "engenn6le11ob04re2img03.jpg", "time": "55000", "id": 3, "text": "So the next time you are reaching for the chocolate croissant or feeling cranky and craving a cookie, try these tips above. You may surprise yourself!"}], "audiosrc": "engenn6le11ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le11ob04re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"co